// @test: typecheck-fail
// @level: L0
// @tier: 0
// @tags: verification, refinement, soundness, substitution, smt
// @expected-error: E500
// @expected-error: E500
// @expected-error: E500
// @expected-error: E500
// @expected-error-count: 4
//
// Pin (T0789) — substituting the refinement's subject must reach EVERY node
// of the predicate, not the handful the walk happened to list.
//
// `substitute_in_expr` reached 23 of the language's 73 expression forms and
// returned the node untouched for the other 50.  So in
//
//     Int{ (it, 0).0 >= 10 }
//
// `it` was never replaced by the value being checked.  The predicate handed
// to the solver still spoke about an unbound `it`, the solver answered
// `unknown`, and an unknown verdict was accepted in silence: the refinement
// advertised a constraint that nothing enforced.  `Int{it >= 10}` — the same
// constraint without the projection — failed correctly, which is what kept
// this invisible.
//
// The gap was never in the shape of the tuple.  It was that the walk stopped
// AT THE PROJECTION, exactly as the termination checker's walk did (T0786):
// `Tuple` was listed, `TupleIndex` was not, so nothing ever descended far
// enough to find the tuple that was handled.  `Paren`, `Cast`, `NamedArg`,
// `Pipeline`, `NullCoalesce` and `Try` were absorbed by the same wildcard.
//
// The fix is not another list.  The read-only expression walk in the AST
// crate already covers all 73 forms with no wildcard; what was missing was a
// mutable twin for rewriters, so each rewriter had rolled its own partial
// copy.  There is now one shared child walk, and this file is its
// behavioural pin.
//
// The four errors below are the cases the solver can now DECIDE; each has a
// satisfied twin in `refinement_substitution_satisfied.vr` that must stay
// silent, because a fix that reported every refinement would also pass a
// file that only counts errors.

type Projected  is { v: Int{(it, 0).0 >= 10} };
type Nested     is { v: Int{((it, 0).0, 0).0 >= 10} };
type Parens     is { v: Int{((it)) >= 10} };
type ConstSlot  is { v: Int{(0, it).1 >= 10} };

fn main() {
    let a = Projected { v: 1 };
    let b = Nested { v: 1 };
    let c = Parens { v: 1 };
    let d = ConstSlot { v: 1 };
    print(a.v + b.v + c.v + d.v);
}
